#: templates/index.html:181
msgid ""
"A ride opportunity indicator, based on rain, wind, day/night, extreme "
"temps and risk of ice. The higher the number, the worse the conditions "
"and the more dangerous the ride."
msgstr ""
"Indicateur d’opportunité de sortie à vélo, basée sur la pluie, le vent, "
"le jour/nuit, les températures extrêmes et le risque de verglas. Plus le "
"nombre est haut, plus les conditions sont mauvaises et plus le danger "
"augmente."

#: templates/index.html:182
#, fuzzy
msgid "See source code <code>def get_proba_properties(hour):</code> for details."
msgstr ""
"Regardez dans le code source <code>def proba_value(hour):</code> pour "
"avoir des détails."

#: templates/index.html:183
msgid "Linear gradient from 0 (green) to 40 (red)."
msgstr "Dégradé linéaire de 0 (vert) à 100 (rouge)."

#: templates/index.html:185
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Wind speed in kilometers per hour, shown with the repetiton of the emoji "
"💨. Zero to two is okay, three and four (for speeds above "
"%(max_wind)s<abbr title='kilometers per hour'>kph</abbr>) are strong to "
"very strong winds."
msgstr ""
"Vitesse du vent en kilomètres par heure, montrée par la répétition de "
"l’emoji 💨. Jusqu’à deux le vent est supportable, à trois ou quatre "
"(vitesses au delà de %(max_wind)s&nbsp;<abbr title='kilomètres "
"heure'>km/h</abbr>) le vent est fort à très fort."

#: templates/index.html:186
msgid "Wind directions, in degrees."
msgstr "Direction du vent."

#: templates/index.html:188
msgid "Precipitation in millimeters per hour."
msgstr "Précipitation en millimètres par heure."

#: templates/index.html:189
#, python-format
msgid "Vertical scale from 0 to %(max_rain)s<abbr title='millimeters'>mm</abbr>."
msgstr ""
"Échelle verticale de 0 à %(max_rain)s&nbsp;<abbr "
"title='millimètres'>mm</abbr>."

#: templates/index.html:190
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Temperature in degree Celcius. Scale from %(extreme_min)s<abbr "
"title='degrees Celcius'>°C</abbr> (blue) to %(ideal_min)s<abbr "
"title='degrees Celcius'>°C</abbr> (white) and from %(ideal_max)s<abbr "
"title='degrees Celcius'>°C</abbr> to %(extreme_max)s<abbr title='degrees "
"Celcius'>°C</abbr> (orange)."
msgstr ""
"Température en degré Celcius. L’échelle va de %(extreme_min)s&nbsp;<abbr "
"title='degré Celcius'>°C</abbr> (bleu) à %(ideal_min)s&nbsp;<abbr "
"title='degré Celcius'>°C</abbr> (blanc), puis de %(ideal_max)s&nbsp;<abbr"
" title='degré Celcius'>°C</abbr> à %(extreme_max)s&nbsp;<abbr "
"title='degré Celcius'>°C</abbr> (orange)."

#: templates/index.html:191
msgid "Apparent temperature, in degree Celcius. Same scale as temperature."
msgstr "Température ressentie, en degré Celcius. Même échelle que la température."

#: templates/index.html:198
msgid "Settings"
msgstr "Réglages"

#: templates/index.html:201
msgid "Saved!"
msgstr "Enregistré&nbsp;!"

#: templates/index.html:209
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The ideal temperature range is based on last weeks weather, from "
"%(ideal_min)s<abbr title='degrees Celcius'>°C</abbr> to "
"%(ideal_max)s<abbr title='degrees Celcius'>°C</abbr>"
msgstr ""
"La plage de températures idéales se base sur la météo de la semaine "
"dernière, de %(ideal_min)s&nbsp;<abbr title='degrés Celcius'>°C</abbr> à "
"%(ideal_max)s&nbsp;<abbr title='degrés Celcius'>°C</abbr>"

#: templates/index.html:211
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The ideal temperature range is the default setting, from "
"%(ideal_min)s<abbr title='degrees Celcius'>°C</abbr> to "
"%(ideal_max)s<abbr title='degrees Celcius'>°C</abbr>"
msgstr ""
"La plage de températures idéales par défaut est utilisée, de "
"%(ideal_min)s&nbsp;<abbr title='degrés Celcius'>°C</abbr> à "
"%(ideal_max)s&nbsp;<abbr title='degrés Celcius'>°C</abbr>"

#: templates/index.html:217
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Use the default ideal temperature range between %(ideal_min)s<abbr "
"title='degrees Celcius'>°C</abbr> and %(ideal_max)s<abbr title='degrees "
"Celcius'>°C</abbr>"
msgstr ""
"Utiliser la plage de températures idéales par défaut, de "
"%(ideal_min)s&nbsp;<abbr title='degrés Celcius'>°C</abbr> à "
"%(ideal_max)s&nbsp;<abbr title='degrés Celcius'>°C</abbr>"

#: templates/index.html:219
msgid "Base the ideal temperature range on last week’s weather"
msgstr "Baser la plage de températures idéales sur la météo de la semaine dernière"

